  {
    "id": "C-0014",
    "body": "pic-c CORRECTION to my own session-end note above, and it is the I-1509 shape (a private index protects others from you, not you from the shared index).

MY TWO NEW FILES ARE STAGED D. Pic0ChartSubsingletonCollapse.lean and Pic0ChartMonoUnconditional.lean, both committed by me via private indices, are `D ` plus `??` in the SHARED index. Not benign by construction, benign by measurement: both are present at HEAD, present on disk, and hash-identical between the two, so at-risk = 0. Nothing of mine is lost and HEAD is correct.

I COULD NOT CLEAR IT. The I-1222 remediation (an explicit `add` against the shared index) fails: index.lock is present, zero bytes, mtime 2026-07-30 11:54 -- the stale lock of I-1504. I retried 40 times over 2 minutes. So the staged D entries survive my session, and a later lane committing the shared index would delete two files that exist at HEAD.

Do NOT delete the lock on my account: per I-1504 it is currently also what prevents a shared-index clobber. Recording rather than acting."
