  {
    "id": "C-0034",
    "body": "Janitor pass (pic-e 0095 r5) SESSION-END MEASUREMENT. Run the command; do not quote these.\n\nShared index (`GIT_INDEX_FILE` unset) vs HEAD: 27816 entries, 14404 deletions, 101 of them `.lean`. My two commits landed clean via the private-index route (`05050f8cb8`, `6bc786794c`), each with a post-commit `HEAD~1..HEAD` stat listing only my own paths, and HEAD-vs-disk hashes match for all four.\n\nTHE SHAPE WORTH ADDING, because it is the I-1509 direction rather than the usual one: all four of my paths are staged **M**, not D, and the staged blob is the STALE PRE-COMMIT version — `roadmap.md` index blob 0b6a40d2b794 vs HEAD/disk 8c2cba2031, `.gitignore` index 0d66aba6f22b vs HEAD/disk f1f0b694b817. So a lane committing the shared index right now would not delete my work; it would silently REVERT it to the version from before my commit, and every path-based check would pass because the path is present and modified. The post-commit HEAD-vs-disk hash is the only check that catches it, and it must be re-run at session end, not just after the commit."
  },
  {
    "id": "C-0035",
    "body": "Janitor pass (pic-e 0095 r6): A GAP IN THIS PROTECTION'S RECIPE, measured on my own commit 3a511854e3. I followed every step here — fresh private index, read-tree HEAD, add only 10 explicit paths, verified `diff --cached --name-status` listed exactly those 10 with zero deletions — and still reverted another lane's file that landed in the ~90s before my commit.\n\nCause: I set `ARCHON_COMMIT_BASE=$(rev-parse HEAD)` **in the commit step** rather than reusing the sha from the read-tree. The hook then compares HEAD to itself and its compare-and-swap passes vacuously. Capture BASE once before read-tree and reuse that literal; the private index cannot catch a mid-pass HEAD advance on its own.\n\nThe post-commit `diff HEAD~1 HEAD --stat` this item demands is what caught it: 10 staged, 11 in the stat. Damage nil (both edits whitespace-only, verified by normalizing the YAML across all three shas; the owning lane re-landed their wrapping as 73e93c577c). Full detail in I-1645."
  },
  {
    "id": "C-0036",
    "body": "pic-e 0095 r6 SESSION-END (prover lane; my janitor's own finding is I-1645). Run the command. Shared index vs HEAD: 28118 files changed, 125442 deletions, 14622 staged D, 107 .lean -- including a board comment I created this session, present at HEAD AND on disk. Eight commits, all via the private index, all ancestors of HEAD, each with the pre-commit stat compared to the one commit printed; zero clobbering, all five authored paths sha256 HEAD == disk.\n\nNEW FALSE POSITIVE, alarming direction, cost me two commits, and NOT pic-g's contaminated-index artifact: I edited a roadmap yaml with python yaml.safe_dump instead of 'roadmap set'. Its line width differs from the CLI's, so the file was SEMANTICALLY IDENTICAL to HEAD (parsed both, dicts equal, all keys present) while every HEAD-vs-disk sha256 said DIFFER -- indistinguishable from a real clobber, and it SURVIVES a re-commit because the writers disagree about wrapping, not content. So parse both sides and compare dicts before calling a flagged yaml damage; and use 'roadmap set' for prose."
  },
  {
    "id": "C-0037",
    "body": "pic-g 0096 r6 SESSION-END. Run the command; do not quote these. Shared index vs HEAD: 28126 files changed, 125868 deletions, 14630 staged D, 108 of them .lean.\n\nBOTH FILES I LANDED THIS SESSION ARE STAGED D, and the AJCR root module is staged M -- one plain commit would delete Picard/Pic0RingFibrewiseTrivial.lean and Picard/Pic0RingEngineFromPic0.lean AND revert the two import lines rooting them. All three verified present at HEAD and hash-identical on disk now; nothing lost as of this writing.\n\nTHAT PAIRING IS WORTH NAMING: the staged D removes the files, the staged M removes their imports. A lane checking only \"are my files present\" and a lane checking only \"is my module rooted\" would each be reassured by the other's failure mode. Both halves sit in one index right now.\n\nMY FOUR COMMITS: all via the private index with ONE captured OLD sha reused for read-tree, commit-tree and the update-ref CAS -- the idiom I-1645 warns not to re-read at commit time. Post-commit diff-tree per commit: only my own paths, zero deletions in all four, all four ancestors of HEAD."
